Changed the automatic REST API queryset optimization to `prefetch_related` foreign-key serializer fields at depth 0 instead of `select_related`-ing them, and to cover the full requested nesting depth (`?depth>=1`) with prefixed prefetches (bounded by a lookup budget), including prefetches declared by the nested models themselves. The hyperlinked representation never reads the joined row, and other consumers (natural keys, `display`, method fields) remain query-free via the prefetch cache — while each related row is now fetched once per page instead of being duplicated into every row of a JOIN. For relation-heavy models this dominated list response time (Devices ~2.5x faster; a 100-row Circuits list at depth=1 dropped from over 2,000 queries to 23). Relations explicitly `select_related` on a viewset's queryset are left as JOINs.
